  "curationSourceHash": "9303998abbc754d7f9eef56a6ab5d114b1e7b1fc67de01c13648c743f240bc0c",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-21T22:05:33.715Z",
  "summary": "## Pylon Toolkit\n\nArcade toolkit for interacting with [Pylon](https://usepylon.com), a customer support platform. Enables LLMs to manage issues, teams, users, and contacts programmatically.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- **Issue management**: Retrieve, list, filter, assign, update status, and add internal notes to issues; filtering supports state, assignee, team, and tags.\n- **Issue search**: BM25-ranked keyword search across titles and descriptions (indexes up to 400 issues from the last 30 days); supports word stems (`auth`, `config`) and `AND`/`OR`/`NOT` operators.\n- **Team and user management**: List all teams and workspace users; retrieve detailed team info including members; search users by name via fuzzy matching.\n- **Contact management**: List and search contacts by name or email using fuzzy matching.\n- **Identity**: Resolve the authenticated API token owner via `WhoAmI` (returns the service account profile, not the acting human user).\n\n## Secrets\n\n`PYLON_API_TOKEN` — A Pylon API token used to authenticate all requests. This is an API token (not a personal user credential), so it acts as a service account; `WhoAmI` will return this account's profile. To obtain it, log into your Pylon workspace, navigate to **Settings → API**, and generate a new API token. The token must have sufficient permissions to read and write issues, teams, users, and contacts within your workspace.\n\nFor guidance on configuring secrets in Arcade, see the [Arcade secrets docs](https://docs.arcade.dev/en/guides/create-tools/tool-basics/create-tool-secrets). You can also manage secrets directly in the [Arcade dashboard](https://api.arcade.dev/dashboard/auth/secrets)."
